{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization 2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","fileName":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization 2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","fileName":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization","heading":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A 2D track can move a replacement element with a photographed feature. The same motion can be inverted to hold the feature still for paint or other repairs; applying the original motion again returns the repaired image to the shot. The book distinguishes this stabilization and destabilization workflow from simply leaving the shot stabilized. For manual alignment, a still over moving footage in Difference blend mode becomes darkest when the images coincide, offering a visual check for a keyframed track. See [[One-Point and Two-Point Tracking]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization 2 d matchmove and inverse stabilization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","fileName":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2D Matchmove and Inverse Stabilization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","One-Point and Two-Point Tracking","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}